{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And of Levi he said: Your tumim, etc.</b> Meaning, this matter shall be fulfilled in his hand and in his seed after him — an eternal priesthood." "<b>Whom You tested at Massah.</b> Meaning, since Jacob said of Levi, together with Simeon: ״כְּלֵי חָמָס etc. אָרוּר אַפָּם כִּי עָז״ etc. (Genesis 49:5,7), therefore he said that Levi was tested, that he is not a man of anger and fury — he was tested at Massah. That is, not that HaShem tested him, but that He saw in him a test: for all the tribes of Israel tested HaShem, as it is written (Exodus 17:7): ״וְעַל נַסּוֹתָם אֶת ה׳״, but not so Levi. From this you learn that their wrath had subsided."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:03.939515059Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}